    <!-- Article 11: legacy article, relinked from orphaned /blogs/news -->
    {% comment %}
      Two independent bugs kept this card from rendering:
      1. blog.articles doesn't respect a for-loop's `limit:` (unlike collection.products)
         — it only fetches the blog's default page size unless wrapped in {% paginate %}.
         This article is the oldest of the 11 in the News blog (published 2026-08-06 vs.
         2026-08-19 for the rest), so it fell outside that default fetch window. Fixed by
         wrapping in {% paginate %} with a size above the blog's article count (confirmed
         via debug output: paginate.items=11, all 11 handles present).
         https://shopify.dev/docs/storefronts/themes/best-practices/performance/limit-product-queries-with-pagination
      2. blog_article.handle returns the blog-scoped form ("news/how-to-choose-your-first-
         sex-toy"), not the bare article handle — confirmed via the same debug output — so
         the `== 'how-to-choose-your-first-sex-toy'` equality check never matched. Fixed
         with `contains` instead of `==`, which matches regardless of the blog-handle
         prefix and is still unique to this one article's handle.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% if blogs['news'] != blank %}
      {% paginate blogs['news'].articles by 20 %}
        {% for blog_article in blogs['news'].articles %}
          {% if blog_article.handle contains 'how-to-choose-your-first-sex-toy' %}
          <a href="{{ blog_article.url }}" class="luxury-blog-card">
